After HeNryous's patch 0033b (github.com/HeNryous/deepseek-v41-1017-dgx-spark, patches/0033b-dsv41-indexer-buffer.patch
at cef176c, Apache-2.0: "indexer prefill buffer factor 8 instead of 40"), our rework; against vLLM main 6e517b15 +
patches 0001-0024 (0001 touches the same file, other lines).
The sparse indexer's prefill gather buffer at 8 x max_model_len rows instead of 40 x
(VLLM_INDEXER_PREFILL_BUFFER_FACTOR: default 8, 40 = upstream, under 2 refused at startup). In the profile run every
index layer reserves factor x max_model_len / compress_ratio rows of 132 B (128 fp8 + an fp32 scale) in the target's
lane of the shared workspace, which keeps its largest size for the server's life. V4.1's index layers 20-36 have
compress ratio 1 (one row a token), so at MAX_LEN 262144 the lane held 10,485,760 rows, 1,321 MiB with the 1 MiB top-k
scratch; at 8 it holds 2,097,152 rows, 265 MiB: 1,056 MiB (1.03 GiB) less per rank (from the code, not measured;
HeNryous's -0.32 GiB a rank at 320K equals (40 - 8) x 327,680 x 132 B / 4, V4's ratio-4 layout, not V4.1's). Nothing
else in that lane is larger on GB10: FlashInfer's sparse MLA keeps its own 128 MiB buffer, the routed experts run in the
plugin, and the DSpark drafter (lane 1) has no index layer.
Overflow: the chunker (_split_indexer_prefill_chunks) packs a step's prefills while their rows fit the buffer and takes
a single longer request whole, which would gather past its end; one request is at most max_model_len rows, so no factor
of 2 or more gets there. At our settings (MAX_SEQS 2) a step gathers at most 2 x 262,144 = 524,288 of 2,097,152 rows, so
the chunks are the ones factor 40 makes and results do not change; with more seats, a step the buffer would overflow is
split by request, each chunk inside it. MAX_BATCH (the 2,048-token prefill chunk) bounds query rows, which only the
logits cap (VLLM_SPARSE_INDEXER_MAX_LOGITS_MB) splits. VLLM_DEBUG_WORKSPACE=1 logs the lane's size: 265.00 MB, upstream
1321.00 MB. Test: patches/tests/test_dsv41_memory_caps.py (CPU; vLLM's own chunker when vLLM imports, a copy of it
otherwise).

diff --git a/vllm/v1/attention/backends/mla/indexer.py b/vllm/v1/attention/backends/mla/indexer.py
